    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119-a1">

                <pb facs="0243" n="151" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg151"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cridler to Mr.
                            Johnson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-03-09"><hi rendition="#italic">March 9,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 42.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 38 bis of January 12
                    last and to your telegram of the 2d instant, both relative to proposed
                    concessions of foreshore holdings at Amoy to the Japanese Government, you are
                    instructed to remonstrate against any interference with or discrimination
                    against any legitimate American rights.</p>
                <p>A telegram to this effect has to-day been sent to you.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. W. Cridler</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Third Assistant Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
